      "content": "Physical Divisions of WB"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "West Bengal's topography spans from the Himalayan mountain ranges in the north to the coastal delta region of the Sundarbans in the south.",
        "The Bhagirathi-Hooghly river system serves as the primary drainage axis, dividing the state into North and South Bengal.",
        "Sandakphu, located on the Singalila Ridge, is the highest point in West Bengal at 3,636 metres.",
        "The state hosts vital ecological water bodies, including the East Kolkata Wetlands and Sundarbans Wetland, both designated as Ramsar sites."
      ],
